      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve understandability by: removing unused imports, clarifying variable intent with well-named locals, and restructuring the helper to have an explicit purpose.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed all unused imports, extracted the option parameters into named local variables (`shortName`, `longName`, `firstDescription`, `secondDescription`) to make the intent of the duplicate-overwrite scenario explicit, stored the resolved option in a named variable `resolvedOption`, added clarifying comments explaining the \"last one in wins\" semantics and the string-representation check, and renamed the helper method to `assertStringRepresentationsAreNonNull` to be self-documenting."
